---
// src/pages/services/botox.astro — Botox & injectables. Bundles Dysport, Xeomin (neuromodulators)
// + Sculptra (collagen stimulator) to capture the KD-0 "fort myers" adjacencies.
// Targets: botox near me (83k, KD 21), botox fort myers (200, KD 0), dysport/xeomin/sculptra fort myers.
// ⚕️ Medical director MUST review this page — neuromodulator claims are sensitive. Replace pricing.
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro"; // TODO: your real layout
import SchemaService from "../../components/seo/SchemaService.astro";
import SchemaFAQ from "../../components/seo/SchemaFAQ.astro";
import SchemaBreadcrumb from "../../components/seo/SchemaBreadcrumb.astro";

const title = "Botox, Dysport & Xeomin in Punta Gorda & Fort Myers, FL | House of Rose Aesthetics";
const description =
  "Botox and wrinkle-relaxing injectables at House of Rose Aesthetics — smooth frown lines, forehead lines and crow's feet with Botox, Dysport or Xeomin, plus Sculptra for collagen. Serving Punta Gorda, Port Charlotte, Fort Myers & Cape Coral.";

const faqItems = [
  { q: "How much does Botox cost in Southwest Florida?", a: "Botox is usually priced per unit — commonly about $12 to $15 per unit in our area — and the total depends on how many units your treatment areas need (for example, forehead lines, frown lines and crow's feet). Many clients spend roughly $200 to $500 per visit. We give you an exact quote at your consultation." },
  { q: "How long does Botox last?", a: "Most people enjoy results for about three to four months. With regular treatments, some find results last a bit longer over time. We'll help you plan a maintenance schedule that keeps you looking refreshed." },
  { q: "Does Botox hurt, and is there downtime?", a: "Injections take just a few minutes and feel like tiny pinches — most clients tolerate them easily, and numbing is available. There's essentially no downtime: you can return to your day right away. Avoid rubbing the area, lying flat or vigorous exercise for a few hours as directed." },
  { q: "When will I see Botox results?", a: "You'll typically start to see smoothing within 3 to 5 days, with full results around two weeks. We often schedule a quick check-in so we can fine-tune if needed." },
  { q: "What's the difference between Botox, Dysport and Xeomin?", a: "All three are neuromodulators that relax the muscles that cause expression lines, and all are excellent. They differ slightly in formulation and how quickly they take effect or spread — Dysport can kick in a touch faster and suits larger areas, while Xeomin is a 'pure' formulation with no added proteins. We recommend the best fit for your anatomy and goals." },
  { q: "What is Sculptra, and how is it different from Botox?", a: "Sculptra is not a wrinkle relaxer — it's an injectable collagen stimulator that gradually restores volume and improves skin quality over a series of sessions, with results that build over months. Botox relaxes muscles to soften expression lines; Sculptra rebuilds underlying support. Many clients combine them. Learn more on our dermal fillers page." },
  { q: "Who is a good candidate for Botox?", a: "Healthy adults who want to soften or prevent expression lines are typically great candidates. Neuromodulators aren't recommended during pregnancy or breastfeeding, or with certain neuromuscular conditions. A consultation confirms it's right for you." },
];
---
<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <SchemaService name="Botox & Injectables (Neuromodulators)" description={description} url={Astro.url.href}
    procedureType="Botulinum toxin injection (Botox, Dysport, Xeomin)" bodyLocations={["Forehead", "Glabella", "Around the eyes", "Face"]} />
  <SchemaFAQ items={faqItems} />
  <SchemaBreadcrumb items={[{ name: "Services", url: "/services/" }, { name: "Botox & Injectables", url: "/services/botox/" }]} />

  <article class="service-page">
    <header class="service-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Injectables</p>
      <h1>Botox, Dysport &amp; Xeomin in Punta Gorda &amp; Fort Myers, FL</h1>
      <p class="subhead">Smooth, refreshed and natural — never frozen. Our wrinkle-relaxing injectables soften expression lines while keeping you looking like you.</p>
      <a class="cta" href="/contact/">Book your complimentary consultation</a>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>What are neuromodulators (Botox, Dysport, Xeomin)?</h2>
      <p>Botox, Dysport and Xeomin are <strong>neuromodulators</strong> — purified injectables that temporarily relax the small muscles responsible for expression lines. By softening those movements, they smooth existing lines and help prevent new ones from deepening. It's the most popular non-surgical cosmetic treatment in the world, and our approach is always natural, tailored to your features.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What we treat</h2>
      <ul class="benefit-list">
        <li>Frown lines (the "11s" between the brows)</li>
        <li>Forehead lines</li>
        <li>Crow's feet around the eyes</li>
        <li>Bunny lines on the nose</li>
        <li>A gummy smile or downturned mouth corners</li>
        <li>Jaw slimming and TMJ-related clenching (where appropriate)</li>
        <li>Preventative "baby Botox" for early lines</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Botox vs Dysport vs Xeomin</h2>
      <p>All three are safe, effective neuromodulators — the best one for you depends on your anatomy, goals and how your body responds. <strong>Dysport</strong> can take effect a little faster and spreads nicely across larger areas like the forehead. <strong>Xeomin</strong> is a "naked," highly purified formula with no added proteins. <strong>Botox</strong> is the original and most recognized. We'll recommend the right product at your consultation.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Adding Sculptra for collagen &amp; volume</h2>
      <p>For clients who want to restore lost volume and improve overall skin quality, we also offer <strong>Sculptra</strong> — an injectable that stimulates your own collagen gradually over several months. It's a different tool than a wrinkle relaxer, and it pairs beautifully with Botox for a natural, refreshed result. See our <a href="/services/dermal-fillers/">dermal fillers page</a> for more on volume treatments.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What to expect at House of Rose</h2>
      <p>Your visit starts with a consultation to understand your goals and map your treatment. The injections themselves take only a few minutes. There's no downtime — you'll return to your day right away, with results appearing over the next several days and full effect around two weeks.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Injectables for Charlotte &amp; Lee County</h2>
      <p>House of Rose Aesthetics offers Botox, Dysport, Xeomin and Sculptra throughout Southwest Florida — <strong>Punta Gorda</strong>, <strong>Port Charlotte</strong>, <strong>Fort Myers</strong> and <strong>Cape Coral</strong>. Book a consultation for a natural, personalized plan.</p>
      <a class="cta" href="/contact/">Schedule your consultation</a>
    </section>

    <section class="faq">
      <h2>Botox &amp; Injectables FAQs</h2>
      {faqItems.map((item) => (<details><summary>{item.q}</summary><p>{item.a}</p></details>))}
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .service-page { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.25rem 4rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .service-hero { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .eyebrow { text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .16em; font-size: .78rem; font-weight: 600; opacity: .7; margin: 0 0 .5rem; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 5vw, 2.75rem); line-height: 1.1; margin: 0 0 .8rem; text-wrap: balance; }
  .subhead { font-size: 1.1rem; opacity: .85; margin: 0 0 1.5rem; }
  section { margin-bottom: 2.25rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 0 0 .6rem; }
  .benefit-list { padding-left: 1.2rem; } .benefit-list li { margin-bottom: .4rem; }
  .cta { display: inline-block; padding: .8rem 1.4rem; border-radius: 999px; background: #a23b57; color: #fff; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; }
  .cta:hover { background: #7d2b41; }
  a { color: #a23b57; }
  .faq details { border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.1); padding: .9rem 0; }
  .faq summary { font-weight: 600; cursor: pointer; font-size: 1.02rem; }
  .faq details p { margin: .7rem 0 0; opacity: .85; }
</style>
